# Line endings are LF everywhere, by repository contract rather than by machine configuration.
#
# Without this file the result depends on each developer's core.autocrlf, whose Git-for-Windows
# installer default is `true` — that checks text files out as CRLF, and every tool that then reads
# and rewrites one carries the CRLF back in. Declaring it here makes the outcome the same on every
# checkout: normalize to LF on commit, and write LF into the working tree on checkout.
#
# It matters for the container build too: init-scripts/*.sh run inside the image, and a `#!` line
# ending in CR fails outright with "bad interpreter" rather than misbehaving subtly.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are declared `text` unconditionally rather than left to the `text=auto` above:
# `auto` guesses from content and would treat a script as binary if it ever contained a NUL byte,
# silently dropping the eol guarantee for exactly the files where a stray CR is fatal.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Deliberately absent: any `*.cs text` rule. tests/NeoIPC.Reporting.Tests/SecurityRegressionTests.cs
# contains a NUL byte as a null-byte-injection test vector, so forcing `text` on C# would run
# end-of-line conversion over that file and corrupt the vector the test depends on.
#
# That file's exemption is DECLARED below rather than left to `text=auto`'s content sniffing. Detection
# happens to get it right today, but relying on it is backwards: a stray NUL would then buy any file an
# exemption from the line-ending, BOM and UTF-8 checks, silently, which is the class of corruption the
# hygiene gate exists to catch. So the gate honours the attribute alone, and the attribute has to say it.
tests/NeoIPC.Reporting.Tests/SecurityRegressionTests.cs -text

# Binary files must never be touched by end-of-line conversion. `text=auto` guesses from content and
# is usually right, but a file it misclassifies is corrupted rather than merely reformatted, so the
# formats plausibly stored here are declared explicitly.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.pptx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.snk   binary
